    ],
    "is_startpage": false,
    "parent_id": 0,
    "meta_data": {
      "sharepoint_id": "32",
      "sequence_number": "1",
      "story_uuid": "1d29b03e-75a2-52da-ade3-96f2b45863e5"
    },
    "content": {
      "component": "blog_article",
      "title": "A healthy mind for a healthy mother and baby: fostering adolescent perinatal wellbeing",
      "description": "Kenya has the fourth highest teenage pregnancy rate in the world with the numbers expected to continue rising over the years.",
      "date": "Oct 10, 2022",
      "read_time": "3 min read",
      "author": "Professor Marleen Temmerman",
      "isGlobal": true,
      "banner_image": {
        "fieldtype": "asset",
        "_local": "32-Banner.jpg"
      },
      "thumbnail": {
        "fieldtype": "asset"
      },
      "languages": [],
      "show_share": true,
      "show_similar": true,
      "similar_show_header": true,
      "category": "",
      "isFeatured": null,
      "body": [
        {
          "component": "rich_text",
          "content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pregnancy is often presumed to be a glorious moment in a woman's life. The beauty of giving life is nothing short of magical and the mainstream expectation is that it should be an exhilarating experience. This is probably why babies are termed as \"bundles of joy\". However, the reality is that pregnancy is not always a blessing or a blissful period for everyone, especially adolescents."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Naomi is a 15-year-old single mother of a two-year-old and pregnant with a second child. During her first pregnancy, she was excommunicated from her father's house and forced into an early marriage with the father of the child. The marriage was abusive which forced her to flee her home and run to a neighbour for support. She later became romantically involved with a "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "boda boda",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "italic"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " rider who demanded sex in return for financial favours and gifts. Consequently, she conceived after which he abandoned her upon discovery of the same."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Naomi has had to bear the burden alone at such a tender age. She feels embarrassed to go to the hospital for antenatal care. Moreover, she struggles to get odd jobs to sustain her livelihood and that of her child due to pregnancy fatigue. These challenges have taken a toll on her mental health making her suicidal. She says she hasn't gone through with taking her life because she wonders who will take care of her children."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Kenya has the fourth highest teenage pregnancy rate in the world with the numbers expected to continue rising over the years. As reported by "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "UNESCO",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "https://healtheducationresources.unesco.org/library/documents/teenage-pregnancy-and-motherhood-situation-kenya-county-burden-and-driving",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", one in five female adolescents aged 15-19 in Kenya are either pregnant or already mothers. Out of these, one in two experience mental health disorders during pregnancy and the year after birth, commonly referred to as the perinatal period."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "{pullquote}"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Naomi's story is just the tip of the iceberg, the roots run deeper. Kenya is classified as a low and middle-income country (LMIC). Pregnant adolescents in LMICs experience an increased risk of developing a psychiatric disorder due to the adverse life circumstances they face like family conflict, poor social support, low self-esteem, gender discrimination, exclusion from education, and poverty, just like Naomi. A significant portion of adolescent pregnancies is often unplanned and unintended which leads to mental torture due to perceived and presumed fears of the realities of motherhood."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mental wellbeing during pregnancy and the year after birth is critical to a range of physical, mental, and social outcomes for mothers and infants. According to the "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Royal College of Psychiatrists",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "https://www.rcpsych.ac.uk/mental-health/treatments-and-wellbeing/mental-health-in-pregnancy#:~:text=Untreated%20mental%20illness%20can%20cause%2ca%20baby%27s%20development%20later%20on.",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", mothers who experience depression, the most common perinatal psychiatric disorder, during pregnancy often birth babies with low birthweight. There also is growing evidence that antenatal mental health problems can be the beginning of subsequent mental health problems in a woman's life. It is vital therefore, that interventions to support adolescent girls during this period are made available."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " Aga Khan University's "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Centre of Excellence in Women and Child Health",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "/coe-wch/about/Pages/east-africa.aspx",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", together with partners, has taken up the mantle to address this issue through a research project known as "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "INSPIRE",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "https://www.designinmh.com/inspire",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". The project which kicked off in September 2020, aims to work with young mothers and other key stakeholders to develop a solution to promote the mental well-being of adolescent girls during pregnancy and the year after birth. The study takes place in Kilifi County, south-west Kenya and Tete Province in north-west Mozambique."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "At the end of it all, the project hopes to develop interventions that support adolescent maternal well-being and give adolescent mothers the hope and skills to build a better life for them and their children."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The mother's name changed to protect her privacy",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "italic"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
